[{:db/id "q-327067/field-1/d569d64e1b94dabdc9f89c1070c848c6c96526a20f320d6b4971ae3a32604bcf" :answer/id #uuid "2a3b1cad-960f-5b95-8c49-b3f466a081cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327067/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "3fd6f169-aef9-540e-b3ab-c87e372c8b5f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-327067/field-1/d569d64e1b94dabdc9f89c1070c848c6c96526a20f320d6b4971ae3a32604bcf" :answer-field/choices ["q-327067/field-1/d569d64e1b94dabdc9f89c1070c848c6c96526a20f320d6b4971ae3a32604bcf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-327067/field-2/30c65f95461d7cf832bda679931de2b4099e743d19de1b695cb0707c6a50ede3" :answer/id #uuid "9186927d-9595-5c2e-acd1-153523445455" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327067/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "b18be829-c5e5-53d1-b794-4433f333a7a0" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-327067/field-2/30c65f95461d7cf832bda679931de2b4099e743d19de1b695cb0707c6a50ede3" :answer-field/choices ["q-327067/field-2/30c65f95461d7cf832bda679931de2b4099e743d19de1b695cb0707c6a50ede3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-327067" :question/id #uuid "94fb70fb-6693-5842-96d8-53b4983d8a14" :question/math-academy-id "q-327067" :question/problem "Find the two solutions to the equation $5\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\sqrt{3}=2\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi .$\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$ \n{{field-1}} and $x=$ \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\sqrt{3} & =2\\operatorname{cot}⁡x \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cot}⁡x & =-\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{cot}⁡x & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{3}{-\\sqrt{3}}=-\\sqrt{3}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\text{arctan}(-\\sqrt{3})=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}\n$$\n\nSince $-\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ lies outside the given domain, it is not a solution.\n\nTo generate the solutions, we add integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\pi +x=\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{3}=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}, \\\\ {x}_{2} & =2\\pi +x=2\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{3}=\\frac{5\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are ${x}_{1}=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$ and ${x}_{2}=\\frac{5\\pi }{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-327067/field-1" "q-327067/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ba963ded-e9ff-5324-9d22-acb6b7a85e10"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-327067"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-326456/field-1/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8" :answer/id #uuid "acdb7989-4fe0-5d4d-a819-552e91d17967" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-326456/field-1/23a7b929cccc5bdeb88db3bdc770afbaf59570d63e930fc5c94f26cb6f5091dc" :answer/id #uuid "a2a3fd83-297b-55bf-99b5-24bf187c64dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "60" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-326456/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "5975a918-9dd1-5a91-9bb8-9b3ba13be609" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-326456/field-1/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8" :answer-field/choices ["q-326456/field-1/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8" "q-326456/field-1/23a7b929cccc5bdeb88db3bdc770afbaf59570d63e930fc5c94f26cb6f5091dc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-326456/field-2/407a8c9dd7706a5c0017938bdc16d552cb404ed5280e2197eaee2471cbb5128e" :answer/id #uuid "eda058f7-6eeb-5bc9-a889-86b106b473ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "210" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-326456/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "3f0a89c4-4972-5a78-9bbf-678456cdabd5" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-326456/field-2/407a8c9dd7706a5c0017938bdc16d552cb404ed5280e2197eaee2471cbb5128e" :answer-field/choices ["q-326456/field-2/407a8c9dd7706a5c0017938bdc16d552cb404ed5280e2197eaee2471cbb5128e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-326456" :question/id #uuid "a0fadc36-cf82-5474-9255-b11413dca9c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-326456" :question/problem "Find the two solutions to the equation $3\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-\\sqrt{3}=2\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$ \n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$ and $x=$ \n{{field-2}}${}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-\\sqrt{3} & =2\\operatorname{cot}⁡x \\\\ \\operatorname{cot}⁡x & =\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})={30}^{∘}\n$$\n\nSince ${30}^{∘}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={30}^{∘}.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of ${180}^{∘}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}={180}^{∘}+{30}^{∘}={210}^{∘}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x={30}^{∘}$ and $x={210}^{∘}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-326456/field-1" "q-326456/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ba963ded-e9ff-5324-9d22-acb6b7a85e10"] :k