& =293.199 \\\\  & ≈{293}^{∘},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\neach rounded to the nearest integer.\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x={113}^{∘}$ and $x={293}^{∘}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-274562/field-1" "q-274562/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c71c49ee-e496-5d4e-87fa-96e28dd830ca"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-274562"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-327790/field-1/441f9a41e4c1d7c29719a73a7d795c394ee1337b1a990ebfb59a7b69a254418f" :answer/id #uuid "b80a356c-327e-5265-8518-cfcad5687e87" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327790/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "a2bc3b6f-eba2-50a1-b7b7-fdaf6fc8e501" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-327790/field-1/441f9a41e4c1d7c29719a73a7d795c394ee1337b1a990ebfb59a7b69a254418f" :answer-field/choices ["q-327790/field-1/441f9a41e4c1d7c29719a73a7d795c394ee1337b1a990ebfb59a7b69a254418f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-327790/field-2/e69e46056c61d03ac81fa66e418618e77f184bfb88b9bbf8c04a941cc85eaec1" :answer/id #uuid "68ab632d-06ae-55c1-b6b9-5398225dd1a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327790/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "9d45779a-f730-5b74-a378-80c55503ddb7" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-327790/field-2/e69e46056c61d03ac81fa66e418618e77f184bfb88b9bbf8c04a941cc85eaec1" :answer-field/choices ["q-327790/field-2/e69e46056c61d03ac81fa66e418618e77f184bfb88b9bbf8c04a941cc85eaec1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-327790" :question/id #uuid "d33a131c-42fa-5ae5-84f9-b33cd3339f50" :question/math-academy-id "q-327790" :question/problem "Find, **in ascending order and rounded to one decimal place**, the two solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{5}{4}$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi .$\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$ \n{{field-1}} and $x=$ \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{4}{5}.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{4}{5})=0.674\\,741…≈0.674\\,7\n$$\n\nSince $0.674\\,7$ radians lies inside the given domain, our first solution, rounded to one decimal place, is ${x}_{1}=0.7.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of $\\pi .$\nHence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=\\pi +x=\\pi +0.674\\,7≈3.8,\n$$\n\nrounded to one decimal place.\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=0.7$ and $x=3.8.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-327790/field-1" "q-327790/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c71c49ee-e496-5d4e-87fa-96e28dd830ca"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-327790"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-330672/field-1/08abdcc2ec6e7fbbeb3b4a6c16f0f9fe5103445204be490e7989a83420e467f6" :answer/id #uuid "53fdeea6-c18f-50d8-8e90-bc5228ed3f7a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2.9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330672/field-1/439807d5585b48d42ced16b8185146af0ba13f97f0dbd23012170827d5b67e65" :answer/id #uuid "914e68ff-bbf1-5a1d-917c-5eaf66e852b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-0.3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330672/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "48b437ce-b0ef-5eb9-8a7f-0e44fa034843" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-330672/field-1/08abdcc2ec6e7fbbeb3b4a6c16f0f9fe5103445204be490e7989a83420e467f6" :answer-field/choices ["q-330672/field-1/08abdcc2ec6e7fbbeb3b4a6c16f0f9fe5103445204be490e7989a83420e467f6" "q-330672/field-1/439807d5585b48d42ced16b8185146af0ba13f97f0dbd23012170827d5b67e65"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-330672/field-2/57f1df4deeb63ac8b169c1392105cc1ec886c4a882da47e1d3a4a61ab32f1e2a" :answer/id #uuid "92072a3c-e596-52f1-bc87-2ec14ae5396a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330672/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "8a5b793a-70ed-5351-9cf0-1fa18289bf4d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-330672/field-2/57f1df4deeb63ac8b169c1392105cc1ec886c4a882da47e1d3a4a61ab32f1e2a" :answer-field/choices ["q-330672/field-2/57f1df4deeb63ac8b169c1392105cc1ec886c4a882da47e1d3a4a61ab32f1e2a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-330672" :question/id #uuid "817e1b19-74f8-5646-ae5c-716cd762b4e9" :question/math-academy-id "q-330672" :question/problem "Find, **in ascending order and rounded to one decimal place**, the two solutions to the equation $2\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-1=-2\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+13$ for $-\\pi <x<\\pi .$\n\n**In ascending order**, the solutions are $x=$ \n{{field-1}}\nand $x=$ \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-1 & =-2\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+13 \\\\ 4\\operatorname{cot}⁡x & =14 \\\\ \\operatorname{cot}⁡x & =\\frac{7}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{2}{7}.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{2}{7})=0.278\\,2…≈0.278\n$$\n\nSince $0.278$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution, rounded to one decimal place, is ${x}_{1}=0.3.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add and subtract integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=-\\pi +x=-\\pi +0.278≈-2.9,\n$$\n\nrounded to one decimal place.\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=-2.9$ and $x=0.3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-330672/field-1" "q-330672/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74c9c0f6-034c-5d9c-935a-ca27dec1a648"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-330672"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-29692/selection/deb5aed8398f29a5975d8ef7b1698f489b03142e5a675a18eb7befbb96daa6c6" :answer/id #uuid "eb2933fc-aa05-5bf7-ae2a-e4bcdac8b898" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-0.7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-29692/selection/944bd102bcf3656e303333c33fe84926b24efd2908ebd3d02fa8fb743a916099" :answer/id #uuid "27e11647-1c67-579d-a78b-2ce23fb366dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-0.9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-29692/selection/17c124f1b3ef1647a9eb3e32e36e133739af5a9e4bc800680ba6fa18947c4e0d" :answer/id #uuid "25ebf019-5378-5857-81c5-6e11693695be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-0.6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-29692/selection/d9cc5dd437e49c7465be381f4c81962c927a7201d510206687c1f8ba9b9d8b80" :answer/id #uuid "9f9ab013-c9c8-541a-bdcf-9b36e1a2e95d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1.2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-29692/selection/15ee7994f213b4b15d718ff51a8597a12c4d7ebb8192568a04d381a17409172d" :answer/id #uuid "7663d36c-360a-501b-8ebb-54a3ae9f9bb7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-0.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-29692/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "52c9483b-1927-563e-aeee-f70a6605b9d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-29692/selection/deb5aed8398f29a5975d8ef7b1698f489b03142e5a675a18eb7befbb96daa6c6" :answer-field/choices ["q-29692/selection/deb5aed8398f29a5975d8ef7b1698f489b03142e5a675a18eb7befbb96daa6c6" "q-29692/selection/944bd102bcf3656e303333c33fe84926b24efd2908ebd3d02fa8fb743a916099" "q-29692/selection/17c124f1b3ef1647a9eb3e32e36e133739af5a9e4bc800680ba6fa18947c4e0d" "q-29692/selection/d9cc5dd437e49c7465be381f4c81962c927a7201d510206687c1f8ba9b9d8b80" "q-29692/selection/15ee7994f213b4b15d718ff51a8597a12c4d7ebb8192568a04d381a17409172d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-29692" :question/id #uuid "8fe37897-32fe-50a9-97e1-fcfe920775fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-29692" :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to the equation $3\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+2=-2\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+22$ for $-\\pi <x<\\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ rounded to one decimal place?" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+2 & =-2\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+22 \\\\ 5\\operatorname{cot}⁡x & =20 \\\\ \\operatorname{cot}⁡x & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{1}{4})=0.244\\,978≈0.245\\,0\n$$\n\nSince $0.245\\,0$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=0.245\\,0.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add and subtract integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}=-\\pi +x=-\\pi +0.245\\,0=-2.896\\,6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions are $x=0.245\\,0,-2.896\\,6.$\n\nFinally, the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ is \n\n$$\n0.245\\,0\\cdot (-2.896\\,6)≈-0.7\n$$\n\nrounded to one decimal place." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-29692/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74c9c0f6-034c-5d9c-935a-ca27dec1a648"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-29692"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-330688/field-1/80c26c4fb8ff46833e7ad5ae01eb6661702cb939f8f9cc9a630304978a907562" :answer/id #uuid "4f00ad69-352f-5e00-b08f-445f43c82540" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-153" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330688/field-1/aa4e4239377eb61b8bdf37e9f4374abeb3a1fdeaaf409dc6e37519ad01509799" :answer/id #uuid "2a5f5ec2-56ae-56aa-a673-985d7696cbb2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-27" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330688/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "088dba68-4ced-5d6b-a917-93fd475929a6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-330688/field-1/80c26c4fb8ff46833e7ad5ae01eb6661702cb939f8f9cc9a630304978a907562" :answer-field/choices ["q-330688/field-1/80c26c4fb8ff46833e7ad5ae01eb6661702cb939f8f9cc9a630304978a907562" "q-330688/field-1/aa4e4239377eb61b8bdf37e9f4374abeb3a1fdeaaf409dc6e37519ad01509799"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-330688/field-2/c9ec5d6cdf4e67c7f8bce68475bed400e56bf403f3d09b5928f78b6baa512eab" :answer/id #uuid "bab79a72-753e-54a0-b798-1e547e397f31" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "27" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330688/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "ae1b57bd-9066-5ee1-9d82-0f80c2f0ee14" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-330688/field-2/c9ec5d6cdf4e67c7f8bce68475bed400e56bf403f3d09b5928f78b6baa512eab" :answer-field/choices ["q-330688/field-2/c9ec5d6cdf4e67c7f8bce68475bed400e56bf403f3d09b5928f78b6baa512eab"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-330688" :question/id #uuid "937d6843-1044-57f7-9c8a-53013d229225" :question/math-academy-id "q-330688" :question/problem "Find, **in ascending order and rounded to the nearest integer**, the two solutions to the equation $4\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+6$ for $-{180}^{∘}\\le x<{180}^{∘}.$\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$ \n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$ and $x=$ \n{{field-2}}${}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{cot}⁡x & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+6 \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cot}⁡x & =6 \\\\ \\operatorname{cot}⁡x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})=(26.565\\,0…)^{∘}≈{26.565}^{∘}\n$$\n\nSince ${26.565}^{∘}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution, rounded to the nearest integer, is ${x}_{1}={27}^{∘}.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of ${180}^{∘}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=-{180}^{∘}+x=-{180}^{∘}+{26.565}^{∘}≈-{153}^{∘},\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer.\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x={-153}^{∘}$ and $x={27}^{∘}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-330688/field-1" "q-330688/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74c9c0f6-034c-5d9c-935a-ca27dec1a648"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-330688"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-120630/selection/d9cc5dd437e49c7465be381f4c81962c927a7201d510206687c1f8ba9b9d8b80" :answer/id #uuid "b4789114-b6e4-5b3e-bf5d-f3d13dcc986d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1.2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120630/selection/568478907b5f0ed672a6aad2869b16e5c7f198079f2189d186e48c24d2500cb0" :answer/id #uuid "1b767c32-42b4-56d9-86cf-1ed8de82400b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2.1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120630/selection/90f87bbef6d91555b634b4b5ce0b3f5397035cb8a63db819e4ddf6c38878f78f" :answer/id #uuid "dfe0bb7c-7591-5493-9388-ce809211c419" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120630/selection/a39e4c3855e119cc134cd501616b2d4242dd33fe6134da1d7da0776d673411f7" :answer/id #uuid "fc7ae4af-ccf0-5d23-9379-0a17a4b9879c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-0.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120630/selection/deb5aed8398f29a5975d8ef7b1698f489b03142e5a675a18eb7befbb96daa6c6" :answer/id #uuid "c14adf90-e254-5dcb-9985-622bd442251b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-0.7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120630/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "df01f03e-d7e3-5d8c-bea5-b2ed4495539d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-120630/selection/deb5aed8398f29a5975d8ef7b1698f489b03142e5a675a18eb7befbb96daa6c6" :answer-field/choices ["q-120630/selection/d9cc5dd437e49c7465be381f4c81962c927a7201d510206687c1f8ba9b9d8b80" "q-120630/selection/568478907b5f0ed672a6aad2869b16e5c7f198079f2189d186e48c24d2500cb0" "q-120630/selection/90f87bbef6d91555b634b4b5ce0b3f5397035cb8a63db819e4ddf6c38878f78f" "q-120630/selection/a39e4c3855e119cc134cd501616b2d4242dd33fe6134da1d7da0776d673411f7" "q-120630/selection/deb5aed8398f29a5975d8ef7b1698f489b03142e5a675a18eb7befbb96daa6c6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-120630" :question/id #uuid "7c0b5c78-95de-5a23-ba33-d70ce7c6a566" :question/math-academy-id "q-120630" :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to the equation $4(\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+1)=3\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$ for $-\\pi <x<\\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ rounded to one decimal place?" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+1) & =3\\operatorname{cot}⁡x \\\\ 4\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+4 & =3\\operatorname{cot}⁡x \\\\ \\operatorname{cot}⁡x & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=-\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{1}{4})=-0.244\\,978≈-0.245\\,0\n$$\n\nSince $-0.245\\,0$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=-0.245\\,0.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add and subtract integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}=\\pi +x=\\pi -0.245\\,0≈2.896\\,6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions are $x=-0.245\\,0,2.896\\,6.$\n\nFinally, the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ is \n\n$$\n(-0.245\\,0)\\cdot 2.896\\,6≈-0.7\n$$\n\nrounded to one decimal place." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-120630/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74c9c0f6-034c-5d9c-935a-ca27dec1a648"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-120630"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-29222/selection/c143ca64ec013e5fe4018485f8c456b26425ea6baf2691e509470a46cd90ac4d" :answer/id #uuid "2bc65731-3185-556d-9ae8-34700ae48384" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-29222/selection/cfef9acaa50d52a14758d2e4ae5334697ec046bff180207fd7a693101464c15f" :answer/id #uuid "a7e602d9-e972-5acf-9c8a-f4679aa5f61e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-29222/selection/4474a39579e8640865737ab970e0c30d067a600377b903df4b98790832a3d86e" :answer/id #uuid "280d9d10-2c5a-5a58-9312-43a70a5108de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-29222/selection/dd221a5b7ef1237a7aeca75aa4d60db84c893d8a867c71204034cfd57d0f94e1" :answer/id #uuid "d491bab4-2b85-5bba-acd0-16dfdf998469" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-29222/selection/0d782dc17ff43c02f50a0e3c54713c0f768ac9dfff69730a158d17df7241cb36" :answer/id #uuid "feb606c8-1b16-50c8-97d8-d652064b0290" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-29222/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a3e931e9-3a4c-5b33-96d9-bba777079da1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-29222/selection/dd221a5b7ef1237a7aeca75aa4d60db84c893d8a867c71204034cfd57d0f94e1" :answer-field/choices ["q-29222/selection/c143ca64ec013e5fe4018485f8c456b26425ea6baf2691e509470a46cd90ac4d" "q-29222/selection/cfef9acaa50d52a14758d2e4ae5334697ec046bff180207fd7a693101464c15f" "q-29222/selection/4474a39579e8640865737ab970e0c30d067a600377b903df4b98790832a3d86e" "q-29222/selection/dd221a5b7ef1237a7aeca75aa4d60db84c893d8a867c71204034cfd57d0f94e1" "q-29222/selection/0d782dc17ff43c02f50a0e3c54713c0f768ac9dfff69730a158d17df7241cb36"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-29222" :question/id #uuid "e9d607ea-fb2b-5d04-99a0-145b3d95ff14" :question/math-academy-id "q-29222" :question/problem "Solve the equation $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=-1$ for $0\\le x<\\pi .$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=-1\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-1)=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $-\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ lies outside the given domain, it is not a solution.\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add and subtract integer multiples of ${180}^{∘}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=\\pi +x=\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{4}=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution is $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-29222/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74c9c0f6-034c-5d9c-935a-ca27dec1a648"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-29222"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-80200/selection/104d1e0f57901066548a7bb71acc3e45fb1e67442fc888335c2ad54d838ee95f" :answer/id #uuid "45cbbc7e-3a36-5410-8b17-df56d478cf15" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80200/selection/b627bdd0369562afa8f12be8f167039ff5f7a2bdc550b832dce7f5205e0a89bc" :answer/id #uuid "4610b5fa-7afb-5ab3-ab8c-dc9b551e5eba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80200/selection/6d0ddf4a027d33d63c47ea1e345b94bbfab0dc44fa0fe8d8d79232a294678632" :answer/id #uuid "fb12cba3-85e2-5421-974a-3c533347c99f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80200/selection/85f3cbb03f56df0239b5c275fa820debc828f75e94d3c126a524051aa22a9435" :answer/id #uuid "202ea43e-84a2-5b61-afad-7c6680129da2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3{\\pi }^{2}}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80200/selection/d5e87f1e68e8b2f0806a401174edd630072c64589b18a731c9a8bb75d45bdd4e" :answer/id #uuid "e40d8568-be74-5186-896d-3202579ef4f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80200/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "80531478-53c0-5051-b248-4468d02db2b4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-80200/selection/d5e87f1e68e8b2f0806a401174edd630072c64589b18a731c9a8bb75d45bdd4e" :answer-field/choices ["q-80200/selection/104d1e0f57901066548a7bb71acc3e45fb1e67442fc888335c2ad54d838ee95f" "q-80200/selection/b627bdd0369562afa8f12be8f167039ff5f7a2bdc550b832dce7f5205e0a89bc" "q-80200/selection/6d0ddf4a027d33d63c47ea1e345b94bbfab0dc44fa0fe8d8d79232a294678632" "q-80200/selection/85f3cbb03f56df0239b5c275fa820debc828f75e94d3c126a524051aa22a9435" "q-80200/selection/d5e87f1e68e8b2f0806a401174edd630072c64589b18a731c9a8bb75d45bdd4e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-80200" :question/id #uuid "c2d36579-fcf3-58d1-882f-1fb91ac58539" :question/math-academy-id "q-80200" :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to the equation $7\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-5=-5-3\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$ for $-\\pi <x<\\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to isolate $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-5 & =-5-3\\operatorname{cot}⁡x \\\\ 10\\operatorname{cot}⁡x & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{cot}⁡x & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can't find an equivalent equation involving tangent, since this would lead to us dividing by $0:$\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{1}{0}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nHowever, we can instead find an equivalent equation using the fact that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}=0\n$$\n\nIn this case, we can find the principal solution as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =0 \\\\ x & =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡0 \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this value lies inside the desired domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$\n\nTo find more solutions, we subtract integer multiples of $\\pi $ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={x}_{1}-\\pi  \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\pi  \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our solutions are $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2},-\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\cdot (-\\frac{\\pi }{2})=-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-80200/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6e126b20-0507-5f22-ba34-a55157ca7fa1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80200"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-330722/field-1/f9ce6d2531e925e028befc33f5bb5202bf5c98dc29df5818c58d5bd59c914412" :answer/id #uuid "1744a427-773d-5213-bf4e-d512f4c44454" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "90" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330722/field-1/23191a7abb2085fa58cfcf0bd067eedb8c4feb2e427bc3ee2024594244bb9b18" :answer/id #uuid "ec326b1e-7e40-53f6-ab89-e9ca255b3bc3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "180" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330722/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "784d2ce2-b722-5437-8bcc-6fdb857b977d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-330722/field-1/f9ce6d2531e925e028befc33f5bb5202bf5c98dc29df5818c58d5bd59c914412" :answer-field/choices ["q-330722/field-1/f9ce6d2531e925e028befc33f5bb5202bf5c98dc29df5818c58d5bd59c914412" "q-330722/field-1/23191a7abb2085fa58cfcf0bd067eedb8c4feb2e427bc3ee2024594244bb9b18"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-330722/field-2/1ad763bfa28dd8bf929699f6c31cff536336c19979c6baa533b7a886875a37b7" :answer/id #uuid "83e5412b-a9ee-58bf-9752-01d0fb1baa47" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "270" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330722/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "c57a8a7a-0c9e-5503-9a92-9aeba9a30349" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-330722/field-2/1ad763bfa28dd8bf929699f6c31cff536336c19979c6baa533b7a886875a37b7" :answer-field/choices ["q-330722/field-2/1ad763bfa28dd8bf929699f6c31cff536336c19979c6baa533b7a886875a37b7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-330722" :question/id #uuid "78f73c58-6327-5d33-99f1-a45e67770ab5" :question/math-academy-id "q-330722" :question/problem "Find the two solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\sqrt{18}=3\\sqrt{2}$ for ${0}^{∘}<x<{360}^{∘}.$\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$ \n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$ and $x=$\n{{field-2}}${}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to isolate $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\sqrt{18} & =3\\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{cot}⁡x & =3\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{18} \\\\ \\operatorname{cot}⁡x & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can't find an equivalent equation involving tangent, since this would lead to us dividing by $0:$\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{1}{0}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nHowever, we can instead find an equivalent equation using the fact that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}=0\n$$\n\nIn this case, we can find the principal solution as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =0 \\\\ x & =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡0 \\\\ {x}_{1} & ={90}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this value lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={90}^{∘}.$\n\nTo find more solutions, we add integer multiples of ${180}^{∘}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =x+{180}^{∘}={90}^{∘}+{180}^{∘}={270}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, our solutions are $x={90}^{∘}$ and $x={270}^{∘}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-330722/field-1" "q-330722/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6e126b20-0507-5f22-ba34-a55157ca7fa1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-330722"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-120643/selection/bf68b941a1cdc58fe4bedadfb75da886a393834a0441e100b32da570fd12ef03" :answer/id #uuid "79557bfb-471a-55fa-bc28-c6edaac725ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "27\\,000" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120643/selection/6efe6b401a4d91c44b13aac27c5edcf1a917fdf1abcd99d0018dadf99821fdf1" :answer/id #uuid "305dc2c4-9de9-560a-9702-8fd26fb699bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24\\,300" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120643/selection/76a2e7a61a701c25588fb722989f7e3f4b8f1fb17904d20c0f4d6892b152fb4f" :answer/id #uuid "73e4049b-0526-5cdb-9368-ad59547fbd21" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16\\,200" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120643/selection/eabe062c500d186128ae6e367d4f848832111d5e3cb7338bb62272ee884ec4ba" :answer/id #uuid "88af86cd-5842-5adc-b2ca-90810e8d